      "card_ids": ["C32", "C33", "C11", "C16", "C21"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Tetrahydrouridine has 4.1% human bioavailability and <5% monkey bioavailability, providing additional low-F context for a polar, poorly permeable molecule.",
      "card_ids": ["C15", "C26", "C30"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 Caco-2 permeability records for microcystin-LR, a polar cyclic peptide-like molecule, show low Papp,AB values of 2.2–4.8 ×10⁻⁸ cm/s and Papp,BA values of 4.0–5.1 ×10⁻⁸ cm/s, indicating low passive permeability with mild efflux; this supports the low-absorption component for the query's polar cyclic peptide-like scaffold.",
      "card_ids": ["C53", "C57", "C50", "C56", "C51", "C58", "C52", "C54", "C60"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 oral AUC/Cmax/Tmax records are for unrelated molecules (sodium oxybate, diclofenac, misoprostol, amoxicillin, melatonin) and provide no absolute or relative bioavailability evidence for the query.",
